## Worksheet

**F1 Core loop**: `state` object; `rand()` mulberry32 over `st.rngState`; `endTurnCore()` calls phases in fixed order 1-7. Score 2.

**F2 Map**: `genMap()` builds 64 tiles from `rand(st)`; `canBuild()` checks `b.terr.includes(g.terr)`; `hasAdjTerr` + `b.adj.mult` change yield in `productionPhase`. Score 2.

**F3 Economy**: ore→metal (forge `inp:{ore,power}`), soil+water→food (greenhouse), storage via `capOf`/`addRes`, overflow tracked in `stats.overflow` and logged. Score 2.

**F4 Population**: `addColonist` creates skill/fatigue/morale/job/assign records; `workerMult()` reads `c.skill`,`c.fatigue`,`c.morale` in `productionPhase`. Score 2.

**F5 Needs**: `needsPhase()` consumes food/water per colonist, sets `lastShortage`, applies morale −8; `dm+=3` recovery when fed; morale feeds `workerMult`. Score 2.

**F6 Research**: 10 nodes in `RESEARCH`; `canResearch` enforces `pre`; costs deducted in `buyResearch`; each effect read somewhere (`chainMult`, `stormChance`, `BLD.workshop.req`, `colonistPhase` fmult, `priceOf` barter). Score 2.

**F7 Events**: 12 entries in `EVENTS`; weighted pick via `tw`/`r-=e.w` loop; 5 events (refugees, sickness, wreck, wanderer, festival) offer 3 choices each with distinct `apply()` writes; cooldown via `st.events.cd[ev.id]`. Score 2.

**F8 Trade**: `priceOf()` reads `st.res[k]/cap` and `market.drift[k]` (drifted in `tradePhase`); `buyGood`/`sellGood` both mutate caravan stock and player res. Score 2.

**F9 Hazard**: `stormPhase()` fires on `st.storm.next`, severity `1+turn/25`; damaged buildings skipped in `productionPhase` (zero output until repaired); `forecasting`/`walls`/baffle reduce chance; `tryRepair` costs 2 parts + fatigue. Score 2.

**F10 Save/load**: `JSON.stringify(state)` into `#savebox`; `deserialize()` parses + `validateState()` checks many invariants; errors shown in `#loaderr`. Score 2.

**F11 End conditions**: win/lose both in `advancePhase` (turn>60 check, pop<=0 check); `finalize()` sums pop/research/stockpile/turns/bonus; `renderEnd()` shows summary. Score 2.

**F12 UI**: `renderTabs`/`handleAct('tab')`; log lines carry `l.t` (turn); `data-tip` tooltips everywhere; keydown handles Space and 1-6; `@media(max-width:700px)` reflows layout. Score 2.

**F13 Dev panel**: `runTests()` has 23 real invariant checks (caps, morale/fatigue bounds, prereqs, save round-trip); `runBenchmark()` runs `simGame(seed,200)` headless and prints `stateHash`. Score 2.

**G1**: `chainMult()` reads `st.research.done`, applied via `mult*=rm` in `productionPhase` every relevant tile/turn, visible in tile "notes". Score 4.

**G2**: `needsPhase` shortfall → `fShort/wShort` → morale −8 → `workerMult` uses `c.morale` in output multiplier every production tick. Score 4.

**G3**: `stormPhase` sets `b.damaged=true` → `productionPhase` skips damaged (zero output) → `tryRepair` costs 2 parts+fatigue, clears `damaged` restoring output next turn. Score 4.

**G4**: `priceOf` reads `st.res[k]/capOf` (stockpile) and `market.drift[k]` (random-walked each `tradePhase`). Score 4.

**G5**: refugees/sickness/wreck/wanderer/festival choice `apply()` functions write distinct `st.res`, `st.colonists`, `moraleAll` changes, not just log text. Score 4.

